01,02 $ Basidiomata hard and woody when fresh, functional over several years and showing more than one layer of tubes or more than one year's growth when cut vertically down through the centre; these are mostly big "conks" found on large logs and trunks  -
01,14 $ Basidiomata more or less annual and with only one layer of tubes -
02,0 $ Context and lower surface of basidiomata pinkish or reddish - $ Fomitopsis cajanderi
02,03 $ Context and lower surface of basidiomata not pink -
03,04 $ Context of of basidiomata white or light coloured, varying to buff or ochraceous -
03,08 $ Context of basidiomata distinctly dark in colour, often dark reddish brown -
04,0 $ Context very bitter to the taste - $ Fomitopsis officinalis
04,05 $ Context not bitter -
05,06 $ Tubes in very distinct layers as seen when the basidiomata are cut vertically through the centre -
05,07 $ Tubes not in distinct layers -
06,0 $ Pores angular; basidiomata white above; on hardwoods only, usually maple - $ Oxyporus populinus
06,0 $ Pores circular; basidiomata gray or red above; on either hardwoods or conifers - $ Fomitopsis pinicola
07,0 $ Growing only on living ash trees - $ Perenniporia fraxinophila
07,0 $ Growing on other hosts, living or dead  - $ Fomitopsis pinicola
08,09 $ Always growing on living trees; basidiomata without a distinct upper crust  -
08,11 $ Growing on dead trees; basidiomata sometimes with a distinct crust covering the softer tissues below  -
09,0 $ Growing on conifers  - $ Phellinus pini
09,10 $ Growing on hardwood trees  -
10,0 $ Growing only on living locust trees (Robinia species)  - $ Phellinus robineae
10,0 $ Growing on living oak trees  - $ Phellinus everhartii
11,12 $ Upper surface of basidiomata covered with a hard crust, below which the context is softer  -
11,13 $ Upper surface without a hard crust, but basidiomata hard and woody throughout  -
12,0 $ Basidiomata hoof-shaped, the tubes 2.5 cm or more long, not in definite layers  - $ Fomes fomentarius
12,0 $ Basidiomata not hoof-shaped, the tubes shorter and in very definite layers  - $ Ganoderma applanatum
13,0 $ Tubes in definite annual layers as seen when the basidiomata are cut vertically through the centre; on birches only  - $ Phellinus robustus
13,0 $ Tubes not in definite annual layers; often on other hosts  - $ Phellinus igniarius
14,15 $ Lower surface with sinuous pores or with pores elongated in a radial direction, or with mushroom-like lamellae (gills); basidiomata never stipitate  -
14,28 $ Lower surface with round, angular or tubular pores; basidiomata stipitate or not  -
